# UI page lock

Do not change UI features, layout, navigation, or page organization unless the user **names the page** or **explicitly permits** organization edits after you ask.

## Allowed without asking

- Edit only `ui/views/<page>.py` for a page the user named (e.g. “Feature Explorer” → `ui/views/feature_explorer.py`).
- Bugfixes strictly inside that file.

## Ask first (do not do these on your own)

- Other pages, even as a “needed” follow-on.
- Shared UI: `ui/app.py`, `ui/views/__init__.py`, `ui/artifacts/`, `ui/components/`, nav, tabs, galleries, captions, job chrome used by multiple pages.
- Adding/removing pages, tabs, sections, or moving controls vs figures.
- “While I’m here” restyles or consistency edits on unnamed pages.

## If a named-page fix seems to need shared code

Stop. Ask. Wait for explicit permission. Do not expand scope because it would look better or match another page.

## If the prompt is underdefined

Ask which page and whether organization may change. Do not guess.
